speechtext:
The committee is no doubt familiar with the system by which millers receive payments equal to the difference between 77g cents a bushel and prevailing domestic prices in respect of wheat used in products sold under the price ceiling. Payments are made by the Department of Finance through the Canadian wheat board, and any payments that would contribute to excess profits are required to be refunded.
This additional $8,000,000 is required for three reasons: (1) payments which were not claimed in the last fiscal year have come forward in the present fiscal year and have increased the amount beyond expectations;
(2)	domestic sales of flour have increased somewhat; and (3) most important of all, the domestic price of wheat was advanced recently from $1.25 to $1.55, thus substantially increasing the rate of drawback.
